    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0312" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/485</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-21T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                                1918—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5684. Repeat your 5110, September 18, 11 p.m., regarding Siberian Railway to
                    London and Rome. At same time inquire whether French Government would be willing
                    to instruct its representatives in Great Britain, [Italy], Japan, China, and
                    Vladivostok of its views on this question. If so, request that they do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
